# V1 Component Architecture

Follow these React and UI component patterns used in the V1 codebase.

## 🧩 **Shadcn/ui Pattern**

Components follow the Shadcn/ui architecture in [packages/ui](mdc:packages/ui):

```typescript
// Component with variants using class-variance-authority
import { cva, type VariantProps } from "class-variance-authority";
import { cn } from "../utils";

const buttonVariants = cva(
  "inline-flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-medium",
  {
    variants: {
      variant: {
        default: "bg-primary text-primary-foreground",
        destructive: "bg-destructive text-destructive-foreground",
      },
      size: {
        default: "h-9 px-4 py-2",
        sm: "h-8 px-3 text-xs",
      },
    },
    defaultVariants: {
      variant: "default",
      size: "default",
    },
  }
);

interface ButtonProps extends VariantProps<typeof buttonVariants> {
  children: React.ReactNode;
}

export function Button({ variant, size, children, ...props }: ButtonProps) {
  return (
    <button className={cn(buttonVariants({ variant, size }))} {...props}>
      {children}
    </button>
  );
}
```

## 📦 **UI Package Imports**

Use direct component imports from [packages/ui](mdc:packages/ui):

```typescript
import { Button } from "@v1/ui/button";
import { Card, CardContent } from "@v1/ui/card";
import { Dialog, DialogTrigger } from "@v1/ui/dialog";
import { cn } from "@v1/ui/cn";
```

## 🎨 **Styling Conventions**

- **TailwindCSS**: Use utility classes with mobile-first approach
- **cn() utility**: Always use for conditional classes
- **Design tokens**: Use CSS variables for colors (--primary, --secondary)
- **Responsive**: Mobile-first with sm:, md:, lg: breakpoints

## 🔧 **Component Structure**

```typescript
// 1. Imports
import { forwardRef } from "react";
import { cn } from "@v1/ui/cn";

// 2. Interface  
interface ComponentProps {
  children: React.ReactNode;
  variant?: "default" | "secondary";
}

// 3. Component (prefer function syntax)
export function Component({ children, variant = "default" }: ComponentProps) {
  return (
    <div className={cn("base-classes", variant === "secondary" && "variant-classes")}>
      {children}
    </div>
  );
}

// For forwardRef patterns (form inputs, etc.)
export const Input = forwardRef<HTMLInputElement, InputProps>(
  ({ className, ...props }, ref) => {
    return (
      <input
        ref={ref}
        className={cn("base-input-classes", className)}
        {...props}
      />
    );
  }
);
Input.displayName = "Input";
```

## 🚀 **Performance Patterns**

- **Server Components**: Default to RSC, minimize 'use client'
- **Suspense**: Wrap client components with fallbacks
- **Dynamic imports**: Use for non-critical components
- **Avoid excessive useState/useEffect**: Prefer server-side data
